# AGENTS.md

{{ description.rstrip('.') }}: a uv workspace of labs sharing the `{{ course }}` package. Layout and lab anatomy:
[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Conventions and their reasons:
[CONVENTIONS.md](CONVENTIONS.md), a read-only copy of the conventions guide.

Before committing a change that adds or moves modules, configs, tests, entry points or docs, run the
`conventions-reviewer` subagent (`.claude/agents/`) and fix its MUST findings. `.claude/settings.json` runs
`check-protected` before each edit (files `.gitattributes` marks `protected` are changed at their source),
`check-comments` after it and `review-comments` before you hand back; fix what they report.

## Commands

```bash
make setup                        # uv sync + git hooks
make check                        # ruff, pyright, pytest (shared package and every lab)
make lab N=002 TOPIC=spark        # new lab, always through the template
make configs                      # regenerate labs/*/config/ after changing a lab schema
uv run labs/<lab>/scripts/run.py  # run a lab step; Hydra overrides as key=value
make report LAB=002               # build the PDF in Docker
```

## Rules that tools do not check

- Shared helpers go in `src/{{ course }}/`, never copied between labs. `src/nuikit/` comes from the template: never
  edit it here.
- A lab's parameters live in its config schema (`Field(default=..., description=...)`), never as constants in code;
  `config/defaults/` is generated, never edited by hand; `config/run.yaml` holds the lab's choices.
- Scripts are thin: load config, call pure functions from `src/labNNN/`, write files. Randomness takes the
  `np.random.Generator` that `seed_everything` returns.
- `report.tex` never contains a typed number: use macros from `generated/values.tex`.
- Only `data/raw/` and `report/report.pdf` are committed; everything else regenerates.
- Classes are attrs (`@frozen`/`@define`); config schemas are pydantic.
- Identifiers, comments and docstrings are English; report text may be Ukrainian.
- Comments say only what the code cannot; one-line imperative docstrings.
- Tests check invariants, not numbers copied from config; one subprocess smoke test per script.
- Commits: one line, `feat(labNNN): imperative subject`, standard types, no articles, no body.
